## Workflow

### 1. Understand

Read the relevant code before modifying. Understand the current state of the entity/feature you are working on. Check existing interfaces, services, and handlers.

### 2. Look Up Docs When Needed

When you encounter unfamiliar APIs or need to verify correct usage of a library, use context7 to look up documentation:

1. **Resolve the library**: `mcp__context7__resolve-library-id` with the library name (e.g., {{ if .IsInternal }}"go-chi/chi", "uptrace/bun", "google/wire", "rs/zerolog", "onsi/ginkgo"{{ else }}the libraries your project uses{{ end }})
2. **Query the docs**: `mcp__context7__query-docs` with the resolved library ID and your specific question

{{ if .IsInternal }}**Key libraries to look up when needed**: cobra, chi, Bun ORM, Wire, zerolog, Ginkgo/Gomega.{{ else }}**Key libraries to look up when needed**: look up the libraries your project uses as needed.{{ end }}

> **Important**: If context7 is unavailable, fall back to `.claude/knowledge/` docs and existing codebase patterns. Never block on tool unavailability.

### 3. Implement

- Follow existing patterns in the codebase
- Define interfaces in `internal/domain/interfaces.go` before implementing
- {{ if .IsInternal }}Write Wire providers for new dependencies{{ else }}Write DI providers for new dependencies{{ end }}
- Keep files under 300 lines — split into logical units if approaching
- Wrap all errors with context: `fmt.Errorf("operation: %w", err)`
- {{ if .IsInternal }}Use zerolog for ALL logging — never `fmt.Println` or `log.Println`{{ else }}Use the project's logging library — never `fmt.Println` or `log.Println`{{ end }}

### 4. Verify

```bash
go mod tidy                    # Fix dependencies
make build                     # Must compile
make lint                      # Fix lint issues
{{ if .IsInternal }}wire ./cmd/api                 # Regenerate Wire bindings
{{ if .HasWorker }}wire ./cmd/worker              # Regenerate worker Wire bindings
{{ end }}{{ end }}```

### 5. Report

- List files created or modified
- Summarize what was implemented and why
- Note any decisions made with rationale
- Flag anything that needs testing or review

